  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py` and new tests in `tests/test_money.py`. The full suite passes: 11 tests, including the 5 new ones.\n\nIt works out the base amount for each part, then adds one extra cent to each of the first few parts until the leftover is used up. For example, `split(1000, 3)` gives `[334, 333, 333]` and `split(2, 4)` gives `[1, 1, 0, 0]`. If `parts` is below 1 it raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe tests cover an even split, a split with a remainder, fewer cents than parts, a single part, and `parts` of 0 and -2.\n\nOne case your spec didn't cover: negative amounts. The results still add up, but the extra cents push the first parts toward zero, so `split(-5, 2)` gives `[-2, -3]` rather than `[-3, -2]`. If refunds need the larger negative amounts first, I can change it.",
